    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0439" n="427" xml:id="pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24512: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-25T21:00:00-00:44">September 25,
                            1942—9 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 26—2:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>309. From McBride.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d533-f1"/> Reference Legation’s 308,
                    September 25, 5 p.m.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d533-f2"/> concerning German Consul.
                    Secretary of State Simpson came to see me this evening. He stated that since our
                    conference this morning he had talked with President Barclay who had agreed to
                    proceed with expulsion of German Consul and his assistants. Matter will be
                    submitted to Cabinet next Tuesday. [McBride.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hibbard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
